{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-characteristic-classes-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of quantum characteristic classes","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-characteristic-classes"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-quantum-characteristic-classes-exists"],"tags":["existence","characteristic-classes","cohomology"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumCharClasses.exists","text":"quantum-characteristic-classes-exists.md","leanSource":"quantum-characteristic-classes-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-exists\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-definition\">quantum observable universe</a> with recursive brane tower <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{A_n\\}_{n \\ge 0}</code>. For every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\ge 0</code>, the <a href=\"#def:quantum-characteristic-classes\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting-construction\">quantum characteristic class</a></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\kappa_n \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code></pre>\n<p>exists as a well-defined cohomology class obstructing the lift of the Frobenius--Hopf object of level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>, a global object of the gerbe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_n</code>, to a global object of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_{n+1}</code> along the central extension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1 \\to \\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathfrak{G}_{n+1} \\to \\mathfrak{G}_n \\to 1</code>.</p>\n<p>The class lives in degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> because it obstructs lifting an <em>object</em> of a gerbe. Lifting the gerbe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_n</code> itself along an extension of its band would be obstructed in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^3</code> (Giraud); that is not the question here.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes-exists.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"6.4.5","page":"b/prop-quantum-characteristic-classes-exists","qa":{"counts":{"pass":93,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QuantumCharClasses.exists","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes-exists.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
